<!-- Device markers as Sweet Home 3D 7.5 writes them — phase 0's E6b result,
     and the ground truth phase 1 codes its parser against.

     The first <pieceOfFurniture> is verbatim from ~/sh3d-lab/test-markers.sh3d:
     a marker dragged in from SmartHome.sh3f (tool/sh3d_marker_library.py) whose
     placementKey was typed into the Modify properties dialog and saved by the
     application. Note what that proves: <property> children survive a stock
     save, they sort alphabetically, catalogId carries the SmartHome# creator
     prefix that identifies a marker, and an unrotated piece has no angle
     attribute at all. Width 9.8425 is 10 cm rounded to the nearest 1/8 inch,
     the display unit — sizes are advisory, positions are not.

     The Camera and Thermostat markers and the Hall were added by hand in the
     same shape, so membership across two rooms is exercised. The Kitchen is
     the L-shaped six-point room actually drawn: rectilinear, not rectangular.

     Zero <level> elements, and no object carries a level attribute — a
     one-storey drawing is exactly what SH3D 7.5 emits (see no-levels).
-->
